    "diagnosis": "A model of the microprocessor",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "The microprocessor is a heterotrimeric complex, composed of one DROSHA (in green) and two DGCR8 (in grey) proteins, that is responsible for the cleavage of primary microRNA into pre-microRNA. The functional roles played by different DGCR8 domains (Rhed, dsRBDs, and CTT) are indicated to the right of the DGCR8 proteins. The functional role of DROSHA is indicated to the left of the DROSHA protein. The scissors indicate DROSHA cleavage sites on the primary microRNA. CTT, C-terminal tail region; dsRBDs, double-stranded RNA-binding domains; pri-miMRA, primary microRNA; Rhed, RNA-binding haem domain.",
    "source": "Adapted from an original figure by Maria Apellaniz-Ruiz which was published in several formats, but this figure as it is now is unpublished and was created by Anne-Sophie Chong, a PhD student of Barbara Rivera.",
